# Git workflow

**Handbook:** https://github.com/Khaled-Abdelbaset/engineering-standards/blob/main/docs/GIT_WORKFLOW.md  
**Commit email:** https://github.com/Khaled-Abdelbaset/engineering-standards/blob/main/docs/GIT_IDENTITY.md

## Commits

- Conventional Commits: `feat(scope): …`, `fix(scope): …`, `chore(scope): …`.
- Do **not** commit unless the user explicitly asks. Do **not** `git config`, force-push `main`, or skip hooks.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, `dist/`, `.next/`, or `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`.

## Branches

- Branch from `main`: `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/`.
- No direct commits to `main`; use PRs.

## CI

- Reusable workflow: `Khaled-Abdelbaset/engineering-standards/.github/workflows/reusable-node-ci.yml@v1.0.0`

## Pull requests

- Summary + test plan + cross-repo links when API changes.
- Squash merge to `main`. Backend before frontend on breaking API changes.